   "text": {
    "L1": "India’s cultural roots include old texts, questions, and different schools of thought.",
    "L2": "The Vedas are among India’s oldest texts, but they were not written down at the beginning.",
    "L3": "Rishis, including some women seers, composed them. People memorised and recited them with great precision for centuries.",
    "L4": "There are four Vedas: Rig, Sama, Yajur and Atharva. The Rig Veda is the oldest.",
    "L5": "The Upanishads asked deep questions about the self and ultimate reality. Questions and debate helped ideas grow.",
    "L6": "The Buddha taught the Middle Path between luxury and harsh self-denial. Mahavira, Jainism’s 24th tirthankara, taught ahimsa.",
    "L7": "Both traditions value non-harm and good conduct, while folk and tribal traditions also show respect for nature.",
    "L8": "These connected ideas form part of India’s cultural roots. Now check what you remember."
   },
